.TH FCNTL 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
fcntl \- manipulate file descriptor flags and status flags
.SH LIBRARY
Substrate libc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <fcntl.h>

int fcntl(int fd, int cmd, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR fcntl ()
operates on an existing file descriptor.
Substrate currently implements the basic descriptor and status-flag commands:
.TP
.B F_DUPFD
Duplicate
.I fd
to the lowest-numbered free descriptor greater than or equal to the supplied third argument.
The duplicate shares the same underlying file object and file offset, but its descriptor flags start clear.
.TP
.B F_GETFD
Return the descriptor flags for
.IR fd .
Only
.B FD_CLOEXEC
is currently defined.
.TP
.B F_SETFD
Set the descriptor flags for
.IR fd .
Only
.B FD_CLOEXEC
is honored.
.TP
.B F_GETFL
Return the file status flags and access mode for
.IR fd .
Substrate reports
.BR O_RDONLY ,
.BR O_WRONLY ,
or
.BR O_RDWR ,
plus
.BR O_APPEND
and
.BR O_NONBLOCK
when set.
.TP
.B F_SETFL
Update the mutable file status flags for
.IR fd .
Only
.B O_APPEND
and
.B O_NONBLOCK
are changed; access-mode bits are ignored.
.P
Descriptors marked with
.B FD_CLOEXEC
are closed on successful
.BR execve (2)
for native, Linux, and ELKS execution paths.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success,
.BR fcntl ()
returns a value specific to
.IR cmd .
For
.BR F_DUPFD ,
the new descriptor number is returned.
For the other currently implemented commands, 0 or the requested flag word is returned.
On error, \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EBADF
.I fd
does not name an open file descriptor.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I cmd
is unsupported, or the argument is invalid for that command.
.TP
.B EMFILE
No free descriptor was available for
.BR F_DUPFD .
.SH NOTES
Record locking commands such as
.BR F_GETLK ,
.BR F_SETLK ,
and
.BR F_SETLKW
are not implemented yet.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dup (2),
.BR dup2 (2),
.BR execve (2),
.BR open (2)
